    "detailedDiagnosis": "In Phase 9D.2, section screenshot capture used Page.captureScreenshot with captureBeyondViewport: false on a 900px viewport while requesting heights up to 1800px. Because captureBeyondViewport was false, Chrome rendered only up to 900px and padded the remaining height (height - 900px) with unrendered black buffer. In the actual browser rendering, the page foundation is solid warm ivory (#FAF8F5) with zero black gaps between sections.",
    "mathematicalProof": "Every section image had exactly (clip.height - 900) black rows at the bottom (e.g. Flagship: 1117 - 900 = 217; Curated Collection: 1800 - 900 = 900; Philosophy: 1748 - 900 = 848; Sanctuary: 1800 - 900 = 900; Collections: 1800 - 900 = 900).",
    "correctedCaptureMethod": "In Phase 9D.3, setDeviceMetricsOverride dynamically matches each section height so the entire section is rasterized without clipping or black buffer."
  },
